    "title": "pandas.Timestamp.date — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timestamp.date#\n\n- Timestamp.date()#\n- Returns datetime.date with the same year, month, and day. This method extracts the date component from the Timestamp and returns it as a datetime.date object, discarding the time information. \n  - Returns:\n    - datetime.date\n    - The date part of the Timestamp.\n See also \n  - `Timestamp`\n  - Represents a single timestamp, similar to datetime.\n  - `datetime.datetime.date`\n  - Extract the date component from a datetime object.\n Examples Extract the date from a Timestamp: >>> ts = pd.Timestamp('2023-01-01 10:00:00.00') >>> ts Timestamp('2023-01-01 10:00:00') >>> ts.date() datetime.date(2023, 1, 1)",
